---
export const prerender = true;

import Footer from '../components/landing/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/landing/Header.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service | kgentik"
  description="Terms of Service for kgentik, including acceptable use, as-is service availability, disclaimers, and limitation of liability."
>
  <Header />
  <main class="bg-surface">
    <article class="section-y">
      <div class="site-container max-w-3xl">
        <header class="mb-10">
          <p class="eyebrow mb-4 text-secondary">Legal</p>
          <h1 class="mb-6 font-display text-display text-primary">Terms of Service</h1>
          <p class="text-body-lg text-on-surface-variant">Last updated: May 2, 2026</p>
        </header>

        <div class="rounded-3xl border border-outline-variant bg-white p-6 shadow-sm sm:p-10">
          <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none prose-headings:font-display prose-headings:text-primary prose-a:text-secondary prose-strong:text-primary">
            <p>
              These Terms of Service govern your access to and use of kgentik websites, products, and services
              (the "Service"). By using the Service, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, do not use the
              Service.
            </p>

            <h2>1. The Service</h2>
            <p>
              kgentik provides software, automation, AI-assisted workflows, and digital tools for businesses. The Service
              may include lead handling, marketing support, quote follow-up, review workflows, website-related tools, and
              related features.
            </p>
            <p>
              The Service is provided for general business support only. You remain responsible for reviewing outputs,
              making business decisions, communicating with customers, and complying with laws that apply to your business.
            </p>

            <h2>2. Accounts and Access</h2>
            <p>
              You are responsible for the information you provide, your account access, and any activity that occurs under
              your account. You must not share access in a way that creates security, privacy, or misuse risks.
            </p>

            <h2>3. Acceptable Use</h2>
            <p>You agree not to use the Service to:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>break any law or regulation;</li>
              <li>send spam, deceptive messages, or unlawful marketing communications;</li>
              <li>upload or process data you do not have the right to use;</li>
              <li>interfere with the security, availability, or integrity of the Service;</li>
              <li>reverse engineer, copy, resell, or misuse the Service except as permitted by us in writing.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>4. AI and Automation Outputs</h2>
            <p>
              AI-generated content and automated recommendations may be incomplete, inaccurate, delayed, or unsuitable for
              your circumstances. You are responsible for checking all outputs before relying on them or sending them to
              customers.
            </p>

            <h2>5. Third-Party Services</h2>
            <p>
              The Service may connect to third-party platforms such as messaging tools, advertising platforms, analytics
              providers, payment providers, customer management tools, or Google services. We are not responsible for
              third-party services, their availability, their terms, or their handling of data.
            </p>

            <h2>6. Fees and Plans</h2>
            <p>
              Fees, plan limits, and billing terms may be shown on the website, in an order form, or in another written
              agreement. Unless stated otherwise, fees are non-refundable to the maximum extent permitted by law.
            </p>

            <h2>7. Availability and Changes</h2>
            <p>
              We may change, suspend, or discontinue any part of the Service at any time. We do not guarantee uninterrupted
              availability, error-free operation, specific results, increased sales, search rankings, leads, bookings, or
              revenue.
            </p>

            <h2>8. Disclaimers</h2>
            <p>
              To the maximum extent permitted by law, the Service is provided "as is" and "as available" without warranties
              of any kind, whether express, implied, or statutory. We disclaim warranties of merchantability, fitness for a
              particular purpose, non-infringement, accuracy, reliability, and availability.
            </p>

            <h2>9. Limitation of Liability</h2>
            <p>
              To the maximum extent permitted by law, kgentik will not be liable for indirect, incidental, special,
              consequential, exemplary, or punitive damages, or for lost profits, lost revenue, lost data, lost goodwill, or
              business interruption.
            </p>
            <p>
              To the maximum extent permitted by law, our total liability for any claim relating to the Service is limited
              to the amount you paid to us for the Service in the one month before the event giving rise to the claim, or
              AUD $100 if you have not paid us.
            </p>

            <h2>10. Indemnity</h2>
            <p>
              You agree to indemnify and hold kgentik harmless from claims, losses, damages, liabilities, and expenses
              arising from your use of the Service, your content or data, your breach of these terms, or your violation of
              law or third-party rights.
            </p>

            <h2>11. Termination</h2>
            <p>
              We may suspend or terminate access to the Service at any time if we believe you have breached these terms,
              created risk for us or others, or used the Service in a way we consider inappropriate.
            </p>

            <h2>12. Governing Law</h2>
            <p>
              These terms are governed by the laws of New South Wales, Australia, unless another jurisdiction is required by
              applicable law.
            </p>

            <h2>13. Contact</h2>
            <p>
              Questions about these terms can be sent through the contact options available on the kgentik website.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
